# The source file of this conversion, pinned.
#
# convert_cr26.py reads it from sources/cr_fedramp-consolidated-rules.json
# (git-ignored; the file is not redistributed, see NOT-REDISTRIBUTED.md).
# The Validators workflow downloads it from the base below, checks it against
# this list with `sha256sum -c`, runs the converter into a temporary
# directory, runs the reference validator on the bundle and fails if the two
# coverage reports come out different from the ones in this folder. The
# reports are therefore a reproducible record of one conversion of one
# publication: a change of the kernel, of oscal_conv_lib.py or of the
# converter that would alter them is noticed. The bundle is written and
# checked there and never committed.
#
# The base is the publisher's own tag for publication 2026.11.02.01 in
# github.com/FedRAMP/rules, not a commit id. A tag can be moved by its owner;
# the digest below is what holds the bytes (588,800 of them).
#
# The file is saved in sources/ under the name the list gives it, which is
# the name the converter reads.
#
# base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FedRAMP/rules/2026.11.02.01/
# path: fedramp-consolidated-rules.json
#
782faecae3eee4aa2aa9d32cdb0de4c929524f2e41dc1f3d143a94a9ca64c4e3  cr_fedramp-consolidated-rules.json
